1
00:00:41,968 --> 00:00:45,963
MY ROYAL NEMESIS

2
00:00:48,966 --> 00:00:49,841
<i>Hello?</i>

3
00:00:49,925 --> 00:00:51,426
Where's Shin Seo-ri? Is she with you?

4
00:00:51,510 --> 00:00:53,220
Wait, didn't she go to see you?

5
00:00:53,303 --> 00:00:55,180
<i>They said she left</i>
<i>after her boyfriend called.</i>

6
00:00:55,264 --> 00:00:57,015
-Who said that?
-It wasn't a crew member.

7
00:00:57,099 --> 00:00:58,934
I think it was an extra.

8
00:01:00,143 --> 00:01:01,478
Damn it.

9
00:01:05,899 --> 00:01:06,984
Shin Seo-ri.

10
00:01:09,528 --> 00:01:11,029
Shin Seo-ri, wake up.

11
00:01:11,530 --> 00:01:12,864
Shin Seo-ri.

12
00:01:13,365 --> 00:01:14,366
Shin Seo-ri!

13
00:01:25,252 --> 00:01:26,336
You're okay.

14
00:01:27,671 --> 00:01:28,880
You're okay.

15
00:01:31,883 --> 00:01:33,093
Shin Seo-ri, look at me.

16
00:01:34,052 --> 00:01:35,554
I'm right here.

17
00:01:37,556 --> 00:01:38,682
Who do you think you are?

18
00:01:39,641 --> 00:01:41,101
Who are you to…

19
00:01:48,066 --> 00:01:49,693
What am I supposed to do?

20
00:01:52,237 --> 00:01:54,489
What do you want from me?

21
00:02:17,546 --> 00:02:21,835
EPISODE 12
RECLAIMING LOST TIME

22
00:02:21,975 --> 00:02:23,393
{\an8}She's on her way home?

23
00:02:23,477 --> 00:02:24,811
{\an8}I mean…

24
00:02:24,895 --> 00:02:25,979
{\an8}Hello?

25
00:02:27,189 --> 00:02:28,523
{\an8}You couldn't tell me any sooner?

26
00:02:28,607 --> 00:02:30,692
{\an8}Got me running around in circles.

27
00:02:37,324 --> 00:02:39,785
GONG TAE-WOO AND HAN MIN-HUI EXPECTING

28
00:02:39,868 --> 00:02:41,161
Damn it.

29
00:02:42,412 --> 00:02:44,790
Gong Tae-woo, that bastard.

30
00:02:44,873 --> 00:02:45,999
So much for "anti-marriage."

31
00:02:46,083 --> 00:02:49,252
It hasn't even been two months
since we broke up.

32
00:02:49,336 --> 00:02:50,754
And you got her pregnant?

33
00:03:04,601 --> 00:03:05,811
Ji-hyo.

34
00:03:05,894 --> 00:03:06,812
What?

35
00:03:06,895 --> 00:03:10,107
You have a morning shoot tomorrow.
You shouldn't be doing all this right now.

36
00:03:10,190 --> 00:03:12,984
Baek Gwang-nam?
Shouldn't you be following Shin Seo-ri?

37
00:03:13,068 --> 00:03:15,112
How did you end up here?

38
00:03:15,195 --> 00:03:16,571
Did you put a GPS on me?

39
00:03:18,031 --> 00:03:19,991
You're a celebrity, so act like one.

40
00:03:20,075 --> 00:03:21,410
Have some composure.

41
00:03:21,493 --> 00:03:23,161
Maintain some basic etiquette.

42
00:03:23,245 --> 00:03:25,122
Etiquette, my ass.

43
00:03:25,622 --> 00:03:27,040
Why don't you show some?

44
00:03:27,124 --> 00:03:30,460
I mean, if you're a manager,
you should act like one.

45
00:03:30,544 --> 00:03:32,337
You always talk back.

46
00:03:32,421 --> 00:03:34,506
What, are you…

47
00:03:34,589 --> 00:03:35,882
rich or something?

48
00:03:36,466 --> 00:03:38,051
What are you talking about? Jeez.

49
00:03:38,844 --> 00:03:40,262
Why did you take your socks off?

50
00:03:40,345 --> 00:03:42,180
Gong Tae-woo, I hope you go bald.

51
00:03:42,264 --> 00:03:43,473
Shiny bald head.

52
00:03:43,557 --> 00:03:46,476
Ji-hyo, please get up. Come on.

53
00:03:46,560 --> 00:03:47,519
Let go.

54
00:03:47,602 --> 00:03:49,271
Go sleep at home. Get up. Please.

55
00:03:49,354 --> 00:03:51,398
I live here.

56
00:03:51,481 --> 00:03:52,441
Let me take you home.

57
00:03:52,524 --> 00:03:54,234
I told you I'm buying today.

58
00:03:54,735 --> 00:03:55,902
-Who are you?
-Jeez.

59
00:03:55,986 --> 00:03:57,446
-Hold on.
-Wrong room, I guess.

60
00:04:01,116 --> 00:04:02,242
-Wait.
-What are you doing?

61
00:04:02,325 --> 00:04:05,120
-Wasn't that Yoon Ji-hyo just now?
-Get off. That hurts!

62
00:04:05,203 --> 00:04:07,038
What would Yoon Ji-hyo be doing here?

63
00:04:07,122 --> 00:04:09,458
Who are you? Please leave. Get out.

64
00:04:09,541 --> 00:04:10,542
He said it's not her.

65
00:04:10,625 --> 00:04:12,002
You must've seen wrong.

66
00:04:12,085 --> 00:04:13,253
-It was her.
-Get out.

67
00:04:13,336 --> 00:04:15,330
-Why would Yoon Ji-hyo be here?
-Hey, let go!

68
00:04:15,422 --> 00:04:17,591
-No, babe. It's not her.
-Get off me!

69
00:04:40,989 --> 00:04:42,365
Wake up, Shin Seo-ri.

70
00:04:42,991 --> 00:04:44,075
We're here.

71
00:04:45,118 --> 00:04:46,244
Already?

72
00:04:49,664 --> 00:04:50,665
This is not my house.

73
00:04:50,749 --> 00:04:52,042
Yeah, it's my house.

74
00:04:54,127 --> 00:04:56,671
You're not going anywhere alone today.
Resistance is futile.

75
00:05:12,896 --> 00:05:15,065
It is practically the size of a field.

76
00:05:16,858 --> 00:05:19,945
It would take three days and nights
just to roll across from here to there.

77
00:05:20,487 --> 00:05:21,863
Don't exaggerate.

78
00:05:26,201 --> 00:05:29,079
Namsan Tower looks so huge.

79
00:05:29,162 --> 00:05:31,248
Cha Se-gye,
you have really made it in the world.

80
00:05:31,331 --> 00:05:32,791
It was not all bluff.

81
00:05:34,918 --> 00:05:36,711
But you are destitute now.

82
00:05:38,171 --> 00:05:39,589
Then will this house be seized soon?

83
00:05:39,673 --> 00:05:41,299
Seized? No way.

84
00:05:41,383 --> 00:05:43,260
Who cares if you have
that view of Namsan Tower?

85
00:05:43,343 --> 00:05:44,926
When only a rocky road awaits you.

86
00:05:45,026 --> 00:05:46,471
Who knows when this will be seized?

87
00:05:46,555 --> 00:05:48,557
Might as well take it all in
while I still can.

88
00:05:50,642 --> 00:05:53,478
You're treating me
like I'm some dirt-poor pauper.

89
00:05:54,521 --> 00:05:55,438
So pretty.

90
00:05:55,522 --> 00:05:57,315
Look at it sparkle.

91
00:06:00,360 --> 00:06:02,279
I didn't mean for the invite
to be so slapdash.

92
00:06:02,362 --> 00:06:03,280
But just so you know,

93
00:06:03,363 --> 00:06:05,282
you're the first woman I've brought home.

94
00:06:05,365 --> 00:06:07,909
Think of this as your own home
and make yourself comfortable--

95
00:06:07,993 --> 00:06:09,786
I am already comfortable.
Why would I not be?

96
00:06:09,870 --> 00:06:11,079
Oh, you're already comfortable.

97
00:06:11,162 --> 00:06:12,455
Quick to adapt, as expected.

98
00:06:12,539 --> 00:06:15,250
Right, I am going to lie down
and relax for a bit.

99
00:06:21,548 --> 00:06:23,633
Maybe that's a bit too relaxed?

100
00:06:26,761 --> 00:06:28,388
It's just the two of us here.

101
00:06:38,440 --> 00:06:39,441
Hey.

102
00:06:40,650 --> 00:06:41,651
Well…

103
00:06:42,944 --> 00:06:44,112
Go lie down in the bedroom.

104
00:06:46,323 --> 00:06:48,658
The bed there is plusher
and more comfortable.

105
00:06:48,742 --> 00:06:49,826
Cha Se-gye.

106
00:06:51,036 --> 00:06:53,079
I may have followed you in
because I did not have

107
00:06:53,163 --> 00:06:54,456
the energy to argue with you,

108
00:06:54,539 --> 00:06:56,958
but my heart has yet to give you
consent to go that far.

109
00:06:58,460 --> 00:06:59,628
I see.

110
00:07:02,631 --> 00:07:05,508
Turns out the struggle continues.

111
00:07:18,980 --> 00:07:20,398
<i>Help me!</i>

112
00:07:20,899 --> 00:07:21,983
Help…

113
00:07:24,819 --> 00:07:26,363
<i>What was that?</i>

114
00:07:26,446 --> 00:07:28,406
<i>A childhood memory</i>
<i>from the master of this body?</i>

115
00:07:28,490 --> 00:07:31,534
<i>When your vital energy returns,</i>
<i>it will guide Your Highness's soul.</i>

116
00:07:32,035 --> 00:07:35,747
<i>Is this body already preparing itself</i>
<i>to welcome back its master?</i>

117
00:07:35,830 --> 00:07:38,375
<i>Could that be why dormant memories stir?</i>

118
00:07:39,960 --> 00:07:41,044
What?

119
00:07:42,963 --> 00:07:44,130
Mommy!

120
00:07:45,173 --> 00:07:47,676
-Consent or not, I don't care.
-Hey, Cha Se-gye!

121
00:07:49,010 --> 00:07:50,345
Cha Se-gye.

122
00:07:51,304 --> 00:07:52,639
Cha Se-gye!

123
00:07:53,139 --> 00:07:55,141
I'm doing this day in and day out,

124
00:07:55,225 --> 00:07:56,768
and I can't even make minimum wage.

125
00:07:56,851 --> 00:08:00,146
<i>When, oh when, will I ever</i>

126
00:08:00,230 --> 00:08:03,858
<i>Escape these streets</i>

127
00:08:03,942 --> 00:08:08,154
<i>I'm not asking for a luxury high-rise</i>

128
00:08:08,238 --> 00:08:12,409
<i>Just spare me the monthly room rental life</i>

129
00:08:23,378 --> 00:08:24,796
<i>What is your name?</i>

130
00:08:24,879 --> 00:08:26,506
My name is Dan-sim.

131
00:08:26,589 --> 00:08:27,716
Kang Dan-sim.

132
00:08:31,636 --> 00:08:32,929
Oh my.

133
00:08:33,013 --> 00:08:34,180
Goodness.

134
00:08:34,264 --> 00:08:35,557
What's this now?

135
00:08:35,640 --> 00:08:37,058
Seriously?

136
00:08:37,142 --> 00:08:39,019
Even my <i>hwagyeong</i> has been awakened now?

137
00:08:39,519 --> 00:08:40,937
Jeez.

138
00:08:53,908 --> 00:08:55,201
Stop staring.

139
00:08:55,285 --> 00:08:57,120
A demon has entered your eyes.

140
00:08:57,203 --> 00:08:58,455
Go away, demon.

141
00:08:58,538 --> 00:08:59,664
Shoo.

142
00:09:00,832 --> 00:09:03,251
Talking nonsense again.
You must be feeling better.

143
00:09:04,335 --> 00:09:06,463
Don't worry tonight and get some sleep.

144
00:09:07,797 --> 00:09:09,549
I'll take care of everything tomorrow.

145
00:09:10,967 --> 00:09:12,302
You always say that.

146
00:09:12,385 --> 00:09:14,763
Try finding a man in Korea
more capable than me.

147
00:09:14,846 --> 00:09:17,015
This isn't me talking big. This is a fact.

148
00:09:17,098 --> 00:09:19,142
If you are so capable,
how did you end up destitute?

149
00:09:20,935 --> 00:09:22,103
I'll turn that around too.

150
00:09:22,937 --> 00:09:25,982
I totally blindsided Choi Mun-do today.

151
00:09:26,483 --> 00:09:28,526
You should've seen the look on his face.

152
00:09:30,278 --> 00:09:32,197
No, scrap that. You'll ruin your eyes.

153
00:09:39,704 --> 00:09:41,414
You know, I've been feeling good recently.

154
00:09:43,291 --> 00:09:44,709
Everything hit the fan…

155
00:09:47,253 --> 00:09:48,463
but strangely, I feel good.

156
00:09:50,256 --> 00:09:52,050
Maybe it's because you're by my side?

157
00:09:54,302 --> 00:09:55,553
In hindsight…

158
00:09:57,555 --> 00:09:59,349
I think I needed something to hold on to.

159
00:09:59,891 --> 00:10:01,101
Money, honor,

160
00:10:01,684 --> 00:10:02,560
status.

161
00:10:03,686 --> 00:10:04,687
Things like that.

162
00:10:04,771 --> 00:10:07,315
I had to hold on to something
to feel like I was alive.

163
00:10:07,398 --> 00:10:09,776
Running like a car without brakes,

164
00:10:09,859 --> 00:10:12,153
it felt like I was speeding
through the void.

165
00:10:12,237 --> 00:10:15,490
But after aimlessly drifting,
going nowhere,

166
00:10:15,573 --> 00:10:17,951
and crashing hard, I finally get it.

167
00:10:18,451 --> 00:10:19,661
What's really important.

168
00:10:21,371 --> 00:10:23,957
What I truly need.

169
00:10:25,834 --> 00:10:26,918
I just…

170
00:10:30,672 --> 00:10:32,340
I just need you.

171
00:10:37,804 --> 00:10:40,306
Still, having nothing at all just isn't
a good look for a man.

172
00:10:40,974 --> 00:10:42,142
Just wait a little bit.

173
00:10:42,809 --> 00:10:45,478
Watch me make it back to the top.

174
00:10:47,689 --> 00:10:49,315
Get your hopes up, Shin Seo-ri.

175
00:10:59,409 --> 00:11:00,702
How is the Chairman doing?

176
00:11:00,785 --> 00:11:02,662
<i>He's the same. Still unconscious.</i>

177
00:11:02,745 --> 00:11:04,038
<i>No major changes in vital signs.</i>

178
00:11:04,122 --> 00:11:06,124
I'll contact you immediately
if anything changes.

179
00:11:08,418 --> 00:11:11,171
Actually, you should come right now.

180
00:11:11,254 --> 00:11:12,338
Doctor!

181
00:11:12,881 --> 00:11:14,132
Doctor!

182
00:11:18,678 --> 00:11:19,554
I see.

183
00:11:19,637 --> 00:11:20,805
PRODIGAL SON RETURNS TO CHAIL

184
00:11:23,516 --> 00:11:26,186
If the witness isn't cooperating,

185
00:11:26,269 --> 00:11:29,230
it might be better to issue
an official summons first.

186
00:11:29,314 --> 00:11:32,233
Buy us some time to replace
the head of the resort TF team.

187
00:11:32,317 --> 00:11:35,195
<i>I understand. I'll have it issued</i>
<i>and summon him this week.</i>

188
00:11:35,278 --> 00:11:36,487
All right.

189
00:11:49,709 --> 00:11:52,212
I'm told the Chairman has just woken up.

190
00:11:58,635 --> 00:12:00,136
<i>Seo-ri.</i>

191
00:12:00,220 --> 00:12:02,055
My sweet girl.

192
00:12:46,599 --> 00:12:48,059
Cha Se-gye?

193
00:12:48,142 --> 00:12:49,477
Where are you?

194
00:12:51,271 --> 00:12:52,272
Did you leave?

195
00:13:18,006 --> 00:13:19,674
MY AMAZING FAN

196
00:13:21,342 --> 00:13:22,302
You're awake?

197
00:13:24,554 --> 00:13:25,722
Let's make breakfast.

198
00:13:39,944 --> 00:13:41,779
When did you put this on me?

199
00:13:42,572 --> 00:13:43,614
Who gave you permission?

200
00:13:44,282 --> 00:13:46,534
Well? Do you like it?

201
00:13:47,327 --> 00:13:48,745
Is this some sort of leash?

202
00:13:48,828 --> 00:13:50,538
Hey, who calls that a leash?

203
00:13:50,621 --> 00:13:51,539
Just give it back then.

204
00:13:51,622 --> 00:13:53,291
Who said I did not like it?

205
00:13:56,169 --> 00:13:58,087
Why are you making such a fuss
about breakfast?

206
00:13:59,130 --> 00:14:00,173
I'm a good cook.

207
00:14:02,759 --> 00:14:05,428
My nickname when I studied abroad
was Jang-geum.

208
00:14:05,511 --> 00:14:06,763
Cha Jang-geum.

209
00:14:10,099 --> 00:14:13,144
You said you were Jang-geum,
but I do not see it at all.

210
00:14:14,437 --> 00:14:17,732
For breakfast, you need some hot soup
to warm your stomach.

211
00:14:17,815 --> 00:14:19,650
What is this? It is all dried up.

212
00:14:29,994 --> 00:14:32,038
I knew you'd say that,
so I prepared something else.

213
00:14:32,121 --> 00:14:33,706
How's that for a plot twist?

214
00:14:33,790 --> 00:14:36,751
That's soup from the best restaurant
within the Four Gates.

215
00:14:39,295 --> 00:14:40,463
Ridiculous.

216
00:14:45,635 --> 00:14:46,844
Pretty.

217
00:14:48,971 --> 00:14:50,014
It looks good on you.

218
00:14:50,723 --> 00:14:53,893
I bought this and kept waiting
for the right time to give it to you.

219
00:14:53,976 --> 00:14:55,770
Today's timing was perfect.

220
00:14:58,773 --> 00:15:00,274
When did you even buy this?

221
00:15:00,358 --> 00:15:01,776
Now I feel bad.

222
00:15:02,527 --> 00:15:05,196
I have not really done anything for you.

223
00:15:06,322 --> 00:15:08,574
Seriously? Are you looking down
on my token?

224
00:15:08,658 --> 00:15:10,660
Things have been
pretty tough for me lately.

225
00:15:10,743 --> 00:15:12,453
Little things like that give me comfort.

226
00:15:14,455 --> 00:15:16,749
I've been taking
that herbal tonic regularly too.

227
00:15:20,044 --> 00:15:23,214
Thanks to you, I'm getting both
mental and physical care.

228
00:15:23,297 --> 00:15:24,340
Come on.

229
00:15:29,512 --> 00:15:31,180
If you really feel that bad about it,

230
00:15:31,722 --> 00:15:33,516
I'll give you a chance to make up for it.

231
00:15:35,017 --> 00:15:36,561
I'll look forward to our 100th day.

232
00:15:37,186 --> 00:15:38,438
What?

233
00:15:43,609 --> 00:15:44,485
What?

234
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:47,864
Were you not planning to celebrate it?

235
00:15:51,284 --> 00:15:53,035
That's hurtful.

236
00:15:56,080 --> 00:15:57,582
So, what should we do for our 100th?

237
00:15:58,124 --> 00:15:59,542
That was just a joke.

238
00:16:00,042 --> 00:16:01,627
Just let me know.
I'll prepare everything.

239
00:16:03,880 --> 00:16:04,964
Our 100th day?

240
00:16:05,882 --> 00:16:07,091
Well, you know…

241
00:16:08,134 --> 00:16:09,969
That sort of stuff

242
00:16:10,052 --> 00:16:11,512
used to make me cringe too.

243
00:16:11,596 --> 00:16:13,973
But I thought I'd try it out with you.

244
00:16:18,186 --> 00:16:19,270
What?

245
00:16:21,522 --> 00:16:22,690
Too cheesy?

246
00:16:23,566 --> 00:16:25,485
Is it too childish
if we're not in middle school?

247
00:16:27,528 --> 00:16:28,654
But I…

248
00:16:29,906 --> 00:16:31,574
want to try all of it with you.

249
00:16:37,914 --> 00:16:39,207
Such a fool.

250
00:16:54,680 --> 00:16:56,182
<i>I do not want to lose you.</i>

251
00:16:56,265 --> 00:16:57,850
<i>I want to keep seeing you.</i>

252
00:16:58,434 --> 00:17:00,603
<i>Could you keep smiling like that</i>

253
00:17:01,395 --> 00:17:03,147
<i>even if you knew I would disappear?</i>

254
00:17:16,035 --> 00:17:17,245
CHIEF OF STAFF SON JAE-HAN

255
00:17:19,747 --> 00:17:20,915
Give me a second.

256
00:17:33,803 --> 00:17:34,929
-When?
<i>-Yes.</i>

257
00:17:35,012 --> 00:17:37,265
<i>He woke up at dawn yesterday</i>
<i>and fell back asleep.</i>

258
00:17:37,348 --> 00:17:39,433
<i>He's undergoing</i>
<i>a thorough examination right now.</i>

259
00:17:41,185 --> 00:17:43,437
But why is the hospital
only telling us now?

260
00:17:44,063 --> 00:17:45,731
All right. Have the car ready immediately.

261
00:17:47,567 --> 00:17:50,736
<i>Even today, the ill-omened star</i>
<i>hangs in the Seoul sky.</i>

262
00:17:50,820 --> 00:17:53,906
<i>It appears this red comet,</i>
<i>which had been adorning the Seoul sky</i>

263
00:17:53,990 --> 00:17:56,826
<i>for over three months,</i>
<i>is about to set off on a long journey.</i>

264
00:17:56,909 --> 00:17:59,495
<i>In about 15 days,</i>
<i>it will leave Earth's orbit</i>

265
00:17:59,579 --> 00:18:02,498
<i>and vanish once more</i>
<i>into the unknown darkness</i>

266
00:18:02,582 --> 00:18:04,250
<i>of the far side of the universe.</i>

267
00:18:04,333 --> 00:18:06,836
<i>Vanish into the darkness…</i>

268
00:18:07,503 --> 00:18:10,172
It's a relief
that the Chairman woke up, isn't it?

269
00:18:10,673 --> 00:18:12,174
Yes, it is a relief.

270
00:18:12,258 --> 00:18:14,802
Still, it's comforting to know
that he has you by his side

271
00:18:14,888 --> 00:18:15,889
at a time like this.

272
00:18:15,989 --> 00:18:18,180
He has changed a lot, thanks to you.

273
00:18:19,682 --> 00:18:20,933
He almost seems human now.

274
00:18:21,017 --> 00:18:24,395
He may come across as prickly,
but inside he's really not like that.

275
00:18:24,478 --> 00:18:26,606
He may look thick-skinned
after all that criticism,

276
00:18:26,689 --> 00:18:28,566
but no one ever truly grows numb to that.

277
00:18:28,649 --> 00:18:29,942
He's probably just pretending.

278
00:18:30,026 --> 00:18:31,068
Right.

279
00:18:32,820 --> 00:18:34,113
Never truly numb.

280
00:18:38,117 --> 00:18:39,035
Father!

281
00:18:39,118 --> 00:18:40,453
Father!

282
00:18:40,536 --> 00:18:42,246
-Father!
-I thought you were dying.

283
00:18:42,330 --> 00:18:43,372
Do you even know

284
00:18:43,456 --> 00:18:44,957
-how devastated I was?
-Father.

285
00:18:45,583 --> 00:18:47,335
That hurts, you brat!

286
00:18:47,418 --> 00:18:50,296
Good grief. Did you forget
you're built like a mountain?

287
00:18:51,172 --> 00:18:53,424
Our father is back.
That's our father all right.

288
00:18:53,507 --> 00:18:54,717
Just look at that fiery temper.

289
00:18:54,800 --> 00:18:56,719
All his mental faculties
are as sharp as ever.

290
00:18:57,303 --> 00:18:58,929
All the test results came back clear.

291
00:18:59,555 --> 00:19:00,931
Thank goodness for that.

292
00:19:01,015 --> 00:19:03,809
Everyone was so worried
because you wouldn't wake up.

293
00:19:03,893 --> 00:19:05,186
Hey, Choi Mun-do.

294
00:19:05,269 --> 00:19:08,939
Look at you slapping on
your second face for Father.

295
00:19:09,023 --> 00:19:11,609
Father, don't believe a word
this punk Choi Mun-do says.

296
00:19:11,692 --> 00:19:13,694
If you only knew
the wicked things he did

297
00:19:13,778 --> 00:19:17,031
while you were lying in that bed…

298
00:19:17,114 --> 00:19:19,450
Are you talking
about his interim CEO appointment?

299
00:19:19,533 --> 00:19:21,077
You're already all caught up.

300
00:19:22,244 --> 00:19:24,246
You're finished now.

301
00:19:24,330 --> 00:19:27,875
Mun-do went behind our backs
and got every single executive

302
00:19:27,958 --> 00:19:29,460
in his pocket.

303
00:19:29,543 --> 00:19:31,837
How else could he have gotten that
railroaded through

304
00:19:31,921 --> 00:19:33,839
with a majority that fast?

305
00:19:33,923 --> 00:19:36,133
Now that Father is up and about,

306
00:19:36,217 --> 00:19:39,303
you better not argue and step down
from the CEO position immediately.

307
00:19:39,387 --> 00:19:40,763
Don't let things get ugly.

308
00:19:40,846 --> 00:19:43,474
Why would he? If anything,
it should get ugly for you two.

309
00:19:43,557 --> 00:19:45,518
If you two hadn't made
such a mess of things,

310
00:19:45,601 --> 00:19:48,437
maybe the board wouldn't have
skipped over my own children

311
00:19:48,521 --> 00:19:51,107
to appoint Mun-do as the interim CEO.

312
00:19:51,190 --> 00:19:53,526
You remain clueless
about your own shortcomings,

313
00:19:53,609 --> 00:19:54,860
yet you corner Mun-do!

314
00:19:54,944 --> 00:19:56,278
Father!

315
00:19:56,362 --> 00:19:58,656
You need to listen to me.
You can't trust this punk.

316
00:19:58,739 --> 00:20:00,324
This whole situation right now

317
00:20:00,408 --> 00:20:02,868
was orchestrated by Choi Mun-do.

318
00:20:02,952 --> 00:20:04,161
That's enough!

319
00:20:04,245 --> 00:20:06,455
I can't believe I must claim

320
00:20:06,539 --> 00:20:09,417
you two imbeciles as my children.

321
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:11,252
My goodness.

322
00:20:14,088 --> 00:20:15,631
Grandfather.

323
00:20:15,715 --> 00:20:17,633
Se-gye, you're here.

324
00:20:18,134 --> 00:20:21,053
Se-gye, you should say
something to Grandfather too.

325
00:20:21,137 --> 00:20:22,680
Yeah, Se-gye.

326
00:20:22,763 --> 00:20:25,933
This is your chance to tell him in detail
about all the atrocious things

327
00:20:26,016 --> 00:20:27,184
that punk has done--

328
00:20:27,268 --> 00:20:29,645
When it comes to atrocities,
he's the worst offender.

329
00:20:29,729 --> 00:20:31,397
What? Carcinogens?

330
00:20:31,480 --> 00:20:34,024
Were you so blinded by money
that you sold your conscience?

331
00:20:34,108 --> 00:20:36,569
Even when they all called you
a money-grubber,

332
00:20:36,652 --> 00:20:37,653
I just let it go.

333
00:20:37,737 --> 00:20:40,614
After acting like you're better
than everybody else and walking out,

334
00:20:40,698 --> 00:20:43,284
this is the best you could do?
This seedy little scheme?

335
00:20:43,367 --> 00:20:47,121
Without Mun-do's investment,
you'd have fallen flat on your face, punk!

336
00:20:47,621 --> 00:20:51,041
None of you are qualified
to be CEO or President.

337
00:20:51,584 --> 00:20:53,210
Get out of my sight, the whole lot of you.

338
00:21:06,348 --> 00:21:08,768
Still, I thought blood would run
thicker than water.

339
00:21:08,851 --> 00:21:11,228
Who knew he relied
on Mun-do that much?

340
00:21:12,146 --> 00:21:13,189
Se-gye,

341
00:21:13,272 --> 00:21:15,065
why didn't you speak up in there?

342
00:21:15,149 --> 00:21:16,734
You should've said something.

343
00:21:16,817 --> 00:21:18,861
I guess he has a conscience.

344
00:21:18,944 --> 00:21:21,363
Se-gye, you should know
we were unjustly dragged down

345
00:21:21,447 --> 00:21:22,823
by your sinking ship.

346
00:21:22,907 --> 00:21:24,950
Is Grandfather really okay?

347
00:21:28,162 --> 00:21:29,747
Sensory reactions are normal again,

348
00:21:29,830 --> 00:21:31,582
and the swelling
in the brain has gone down.

349
00:21:31,665 --> 00:21:32,625
What about

350
00:21:33,167 --> 00:21:35,294
the aftereffects you mentioned?

351
00:21:35,377 --> 00:21:39,131
There's a temporary memory gap
of about two weeks before the accident.

352
00:21:39,215 --> 00:21:41,842
But he's recovering well,
so let's keep an eye on it.

353
00:21:41,926 --> 00:21:42,802
Okay.

354
00:21:42,885 --> 00:21:44,470
-Thank you.
-Sure.

355
00:21:51,185 --> 00:21:52,311
Mun-do,

356
00:21:52,394 --> 00:21:54,230
you've been through a lot.

357
00:21:54,939 --> 00:21:57,733
Thanks to you, the company survived.

358
00:21:59,151 --> 00:22:00,402
Not at all, Uncle.

359
00:22:01,737 --> 00:22:03,864
You should also make peace
with the rest of the family.

360
00:22:04,406 --> 00:22:06,325
And give Se-gye a chance
to make things right.

361
00:22:06,408 --> 00:22:08,869
He must have developed
business acumen through his startup.

362
00:22:08,953 --> 00:22:11,330
I'm sure he'll really prove
himself this time.

363
00:22:12,414 --> 00:22:13,791
Yes, sure.

364
00:22:16,043 --> 00:22:18,170
You're absolutely right.

365
00:22:24,385 --> 00:22:25,636
<i>Interim guardian?</i>

366
00:22:25,719 --> 00:22:26,637
Yes.

367
00:22:26,720 --> 00:22:29,515
Your cousin wanted us to contact
the family after daybreak.

368
00:22:29,598 --> 00:22:31,934
And he requested that family visits

369
00:22:32,017 --> 00:22:33,477
be restricted for the time being.

370
00:22:33,561 --> 00:22:35,271
-Unbelievable.
-Though mild,

371
00:22:35,354 --> 00:22:37,106
he is still suffering from aftereffects.

372
00:22:37,189 --> 00:22:39,066
Absolute rest
is the top priority right now,

373
00:22:39,149 --> 00:22:41,443
and as his attending physician,
I am of the same opinion.

374
00:22:48,200 --> 00:22:49,451
How diligent you are,

375
00:22:49,535 --> 00:22:50,828
Choi Mun-do.

376
00:22:55,833 --> 00:22:56,750
FORTUNE TELLING

377
00:22:56,834 --> 00:22:58,919
Why do you look so miserable?

378
00:22:59,003 --> 00:23:01,380
Your Highness, you see…

379
00:23:02,798 --> 00:23:04,550
Your <i>hwagyeong</i> has been awakened? Now?

380
00:23:04,633 --> 00:23:06,468
I know I may look spiritually powerful,

381
00:23:06,552 --> 00:23:08,721
like I could perform a mighty sword dance,

382
00:23:08,804 --> 00:23:10,222
but the truth is,

383
00:23:10,306 --> 00:23:12,182
I'm a sham shaman.

384
00:23:12,266 --> 00:23:14,602
No matter how much I trained
since I was young,

385
00:23:14,685 --> 00:23:16,145
my spiritual eye wouldn't open.

386
00:23:16,228 --> 00:23:17,396
The only thing

387
00:23:18,105 --> 00:23:20,065
that got sharper was my tongue.

388
00:23:20,149 --> 00:23:22,484
I never in a million years imagined

389
00:23:22,568 --> 00:23:24,570
<i>that</i> would suddenly awaken at this age.

390
00:23:25,905 --> 00:23:28,699
For one, you do not look
that spiritually powerful.

391
00:23:29,575 --> 00:23:30,743
Right.

392
00:23:31,327 --> 00:23:32,703
But if you are this faint-hearted…

393
00:23:33,329 --> 00:23:35,789
Your <i>hwagyeong</i> has been awakened,
and you have found your voice.

394
00:23:35,873 --> 00:23:37,291
You will soon be channeling spirits.

395
00:23:40,294 --> 00:23:41,712
Well, for now,

396
00:23:41,795 --> 00:23:43,589
I can only see Your Highness.

397
00:23:43,672 --> 00:23:46,133
It's tolerable for the time being.

398
00:23:46,634 --> 00:23:47,551
You can see me?

399
00:23:47,635 --> 00:23:48,844
Yes.

400
00:23:48,928 --> 00:23:51,680
You were back in Joseon.

401
00:23:51,764 --> 00:23:54,975
You said your name was Kang Dan-sim.

402
00:23:58,145 --> 00:23:59,521
Kang Dan-sim.

403
00:24:02,191 --> 00:24:04,568
I came clutching at straws.

404
00:24:06,528 --> 00:24:07,488
But I am to leave?

405
00:24:08,614 --> 00:24:10,908
So I must have seen
her childhood for a reason.

406
00:24:11,617 --> 00:24:12,743
Her childhood?

407
00:24:12,826 --> 00:24:15,079
I believe it is a childhood memory
of this body's master.

408
00:24:16,538 --> 00:24:19,208
Tangled memories.
Phantom voices out of the blue.

409
00:24:19,291 --> 00:24:20,584
That must mean…

410
00:24:22,461 --> 00:24:24,380
the body's master is on her way back?

411
00:24:24,463 --> 00:24:28,342
That would make sense
if her soul were still alive in Joseon.

412
00:24:28,425 --> 00:24:30,344
But there's no way of knowing.

413
00:24:30,427 --> 00:24:32,805
Who knows if her soul is alive or dead?

414
00:24:32,888 --> 00:24:33,806
She is alive.

415
00:24:33,889 --> 00:24:36,892
My body remains in a deathly trance
back in Joseon.

416
00:24:36,976 --> 00:24:37,893
I see.

417
00:24:37,977 --> 00:24:39,144
That body would not be alive

418
00:24:40,062 --> 00:24:42,189
if it had no soul inside it.

419
00:24:51,824 --> 00:24:53,367
<i>Yes, sure.</i>

420
00:24:53,450 --> 00:24:54,994
You're absolutely right.

421
00:25:01,625 --> 00:25:02,793
Are you insane?

422
00:25:02,876 --> 00:25:04,086
Interim guardian?

423
00:25:04,169 --> 00:25:06,380
Why? This shouldn't come as a surprise.

424
00:25:06,463 --> 00:25:09,925
Uncle trusts me above all,
even bypassing his own immediate family.

425
00:25:10,009 --> 00:25:11,927
Why the sudden fit,
like you had no idea?

426
00:25:12,011 --> 00:25:14,096
That mouth of yours has no lid.

427
00:25:14,638 --> 00:25:17,516
It's time to start minding
that tongue of yours.

428
00:25:17,599 --> 00:25:19,727
Media exposure is
only going to increase from here.

429
00:25:20,394 --> 00:25:22,896
The official Songjin Resort
meeting this week.

430
00:25:22,980 --> 00:25:24,815
Will you be attending?

431
00:25:24,898 --> 00:25:26,567
Of course.

432
00:25:26,650 --> 00:25:28,986
I'm in charge of it.
Why wouldn't I be there?

433
00:25:30,571 --> 00:25:31,572
Yeah, okay.

434
00:25:31,655 --> 00:25:32,990
I'll see you at the meeting then.

435
00:25:40,164 --> 00:25:44,793
DAEBAK BOARDING HOUSE

436
00:25:48,547 --> 00:25:50,424
<i>You were back in Joseon.</i>

437
00:25:50,507 --> 00:25:53,927
You said your name was Kang Dan-sim.

438
00:25:54,011 --> 00:25:55,804
That seals it.

439
00:25:55,888 --> 00:25:57,139
Hey, Rooftop!

440
00:25:57,222 --> 00:25:58,515
Where have you been?

441
00:25:59,183 --> 00:26:00,392
Your place right now…

442
00:26:01,307 --> 00:26:04,897
DIE

443
00:26:04,980 --> 00:26:06,065
When did this happen?

444
00:26:06,148 --> 00:26:08,650
This wasn't here yesterday.

445
00:26:08,734 --> 00:26:11,779
When I came out to shoo away
the birds that kept pooping,

446
00:26:11,862 --> 00:26:13,072
I found it like this.

447
00:26:13,155 --> 00:26:15,657
Maybe there's a curse on the building?

448
00:26:15,741 --> 00:26:17,993
First, the lightbulbs broke,

449
00:26:18,077 --> 00:26:20,245
and now there's graffiti.

450
00:26:20,329 --> 00:26:21,789
The way I see it,

451
00:26:21,872 --> 00:26:24,333
this wasn't done by one of our residents.

452
00:26:24,416 --> 00:26:25,959
It's definitely an outsider's doing.

453
00:26:26,043 --> 00:26:28,212
I should talk to the landlord about this.

454
00:26:28,295 --> 00:26:30,631
Maybe I should request
a door lock for the main entrance?

455
00:26:30,714 --> 00:26:31,840
That will never happen.

456
00:26:31,924 --> 00:26:32,966
Have I been

457
00:26:33,801 --> 00:26:35,010
under surveillance all along?

458
00:26:35,094 --> 00:26:37,221
What? Surveillance?

459
00:26:37,304 --> 00:26:38,388
By who?

460
00:26:48,547 --> 00:26:51,110
DAEBAK BOARDING HOUSE

461
00:26:58,150 --> 00:27:00,714
SPRAY PAINT

462
00:27:00,786 --> 00:27:02,871
This is truly sinister.

463
00:27:02,955 --> 00:27:04,957
What did they even use?
It's not even coming off.

464
00:27:05,040 --> 00:27:06,291
My poor back!

465
00:27:07,459 --> 00:27:09,795
I told you to leave the heavy stuff.

466
00:27:09,878 --> 00:27:11,463
Back injuries are no joke.

467
00:27:11,547 --> 00:27:13,841
We have to move this quickly
so we can sleep. I'm exhausted.

468
00:27:13,924 --> 00:27:15,425
That's why you should move tomorrow.

469
00:27:15,509 --> 00:27:17,594
Why move in the middle of the night?

470
00:27:17,678 --> 00:27:19,263
Would you be able to sleep here?

471
00:27:19,346 --> 00:27:20,681
They even wrote "Die" on the wall.

472
00:27:20,764 --> 00:27:22,850
They could easily bring
a sword to my throat at night.

473
00:27:22,933 --> 00:27:25,018
What if I get unlucky
and end up with a scar?

474
00:27:25,102 --> 00:27:26,311
I am a celebrity, after all.

475
00:27:26,395 --> 00:27:29,106
You go to extremes in everything you do.

476
00:27:29,189 --> 00:27:31,150
You overthink.
Is that why you're an actor?

477
00:27:31,233 --> 00:27:32,192
Stop.

478
00:27:32,276 --> 00:27:34,194
You better watch your mouth.

479
00:27:34,278 --> 00:27:35,863
-What?
-You better not breathe a word

480
00:27:35,946 --> 00:27:37,823
about what happened today
to Cha Se-gye.

481
00:27:37,906 --> 00:27:39,616
I do not want him worried for no reason.

482
00:27:41,410 --> 00:27:43,245
How are single people supposed to cope?

483
00:27:43,328 --> 00:27:45,080
Living in this dirty hell of couples.

484
00:27:45,164 --> 00:27:46,832
I heard Chairman Cha woke up.

485
00:27:47,541 --> 00:27:48,917
-Have you visited?
-No.

486
00:27:49,918 --> 00:27:52,504
Not yet. I had some things to sort out.

487
00:27:52,588 --> 00:27:54,923
Good. I looked into it,
and I hear Chairman Cha is dealing

488
00:27:55,007 --> 00:27:56,842
with some post-accident complications.

489
00:27:56,925 --> 00:27:58,218
Something's not right over there.

490
00:27:58,302 --> 00:27:59,595
I think it'd be best

491
00:28:00,179 --> 00:28:01,555
to wrap it all up now.

492
00:28:01,638 --> 00:28:04,057
That's not what I meant
when I said "sort out."

493
00:28:04,141 --> 00:28:05,726
Really? Then what did you mean?

494
00:28:05,809 --> 00:28:06,935
Mom, do you remember?

495
00:28:07,019 --> 00:28:09,229
Ye-jin, who tutored me
in my senior year of high school.

496
00:28:09,313 --> 00:28:12,149
She attended a top university
despite her poor background.

497
00:28:12,232 --> 00:28:14,109
You used to praise her a lot.

498
00:28:15,736 --> 00:28:18,280
I went to the department store
with a friend after finals,

499
00:28:18,363 --> 00:28:19,948
and I saw her there.

500
00:28:20,032 --> 00:28:22,826
She walked by
while affectionately holding Dad's hand.

501
00:28:23,452 --> 00:28:26,705
When I saw her the next day,
I slapped her, and then she told me

502
00:28:26,788 --> 00:28:27,998
that you knew everything.

503
00:28:28,081 --> 00:28:30,334
That you even paid her
to get lost at the right time.

504
00:28:30,417 --> 00:28:31,543
That's enough.

505
00:28:32,544 --> 00:28:34,880
Between the two of you,
I understood you even less.

506
00:28:34,963 --> 00:28:36,089
Why do you live like that?

507
00:28:36,173 --> 00:28:38,508
How are you okay
with just holding on to an empty shell?

508
00:28:42,971 --> 00:28:44,431
<i>But you know what's funny?</i>

509
00:28:44,514 --> 00:28:47,476
<i>I think I'm starting to understand</i>
<i>why you lived like a fool all these years.</i>

510
00:28:47,559 --> 00:28:49,770
<i>Why you foolishly held on</i>

511
00:28:49,853 --> 00:28:51,521
<i>and couldn't let go.</i>

512
00:28:53,273 --> 00:28:55,442
Grandfather, I'm here.

513
00:28:55,525 --> 00:28:57,319
Gosh. You're here.

514
00:28:58,779 --> 00:29:00,405
I bought some fruit.

515
00:29:01,031 --> 00:29:02,241
My goodness.

516
00:29:02,783 --> 00:29:05,202
-Did you even have time to eat today?
-No.

517
00:29:05,702 --> 00:29:06,787
I haven't yet.

518
00:29:07,913 --> 00:29:09,373
<i>I don't want to let go.</i>

519
00:29:09,915 --> 00:29:11,166
<i>It's so annoying.</i>

520
00:29:12,626 --> 00:29:15,128
It is like reaching for tears
and getting a slap on the face.

521
00:29:17,798 --> 00:29:19,633
This is actually for the better.

522
00:29:19,716 --> 00:29:21,760
It is a good chance
to sort out my next move.

523
00:29:45,909 --> 00:29:48,745
<i>In about 15 days,</i>
<i>it will leave Earth's orbit</i>

524
00:29:48,829 --> 00:29:51,623
<i>and vanish once more</i>
<i>into the unknown darkness</i>

525
00:29:51,707 --> 00:29:53,583
<i>of the far side of the universe.</i>

526
00:29:57,546 --> 00:29:58,630
Fifteen days.

527
00:30:02,384 --> 00:30:04,094
So, what should we do for our 100th day?

528
00:30:04,803 --> 00:30:06,847
Let me know
so I can prepare everything again.

529
00:30:06,930 --> 00:30:08,223
Our 100th day?

530
00:30:10,517 --> 00:30:13,270
Our 100th day will be in the spring
when flowers bloom, right?

531
00:30:13,353 --> 00:30:16,189
Then let us go see
the cornelian cherry flowers.

532
00:30:16,273 --> 00:30:18,233
We can make
some flower pancakes with the flowers.

533
00:30:18,317 --> 00:30:19,276
-Flower pancakes?
-Yeah.

534
00:30:19,943 --> 00:30:23,113
And in the summer,
we can plant trumpet vines in the yard.

535
00:30:23,196 --> 00:30:25,449
Or we can go to the sea
for the beach roses.

536
00:30:25,532 --> 00:30:27,951
Are you possessed
by a flower spirit or something?

537
00:30:28,452 --> 00:30:30,037
You want to see every flower there is.

538
00:30:31,079 --> 00:30:34,166
In the fall, we have to make
flower crowns with chrysanthemums,

539
00:30:34,249 --> 00:30:36,043
so we should plant some in the yard too.

540
00:30:36,585 --> 00:30:37,627
Right?

541
00:30:41,298 --> 00:30:42,257
Don't kid yourself.

542
00:30:49,181 --> 00:30:50,474
That's not you.

543
00:30:52,642 --> 00:30:54,019
You're just a fake.

544
00:30:56,313 --> 00:30:57,647
Get out of my body.

545
00:31:02,069 --> 00:31:04,654
<i>Seo-ri, my sweet girl.</i>

546
00:31:09,659 --> 00:31:12,204
<i>Don't kid yourself. That's not you.</i>

547
00:31:14,039 --> 00:31:15,248
I know.

548
00:31:16,416 --> 00:31:17,876
I do…

549
00:31:21,671 --> 00:31:23,173
<i>I must not dare to hope.</i>

550
00:31:30,497 --> 00:31:33,811
CHA SE-GYE

551
00:31:38,397 --> 00:31:40,649
<i>The caller you are trying</i>
<i>to reach is unavailable…</i>

552
00:31:48,532 --> 00:31:49,408
MISSED CALL
CHA SE-GYE

553
00:31:49,491 --> 00:31:51,868
<i>Call me when you see this.</i>
<i>I'll be waiting.</i>

554
00:31:56,415 --> 00:31:58,166
CHA SE-GYE: CALL ME WHEN YOU SEE THIS

555
00:32:02,712 --> 00:32:04,381
<i>If I leave without a word,</i>

556
00:32:04,965 --> 00:32:06,633
<i>you will also end up waiting for me.</i>

557
00:32:08,093 --> 00:32:10,137
YEONGHWI CHAMBER

558
00:32:14,307 --> 00:32:16,143
<i>Foolishly, just like I had,</i>

559
00:32:17,519 --> 00:32:19,187
<i>you will wait endlessly</i>

560
00:32:20,188 --> 00:32:21,565
<i>as you wither away.</i>

561
00:32:24,776 --> 00:32:27,028
<i>Word has come that the Grand Prince</i>

562
00:32:27,112 --> 00:32:29,364
<i>has breathed his last in exile.</i>

563
00:32:56,141 --> 00:32:58,185
<i>To make sure you smile</i>
<i>when you think of me,</i>

564
00:32:58,685 --> 00:33:00,770
<i>just as I picture you smiling</i>
<i>when I miss you.</i>

565
00:33:04,691 --> 00:33:06,485
<i>I shall convey this heart in full</i>

566
00:33:07,068 --> 00:33:08,653
<i>and hold nothing back.</i>

567
00:33:09,154 --> 00:33:10,906
<i>So you will not wither away alone.</i>

568
00:33:12,282 --> 00:33:13,325
<i>Right.</i>

569
00:33:14,075 --> 00:33:15,619
<i>This is not the time for tears.</i>

570
00:33:18,788 --> 00:33:22,292
{\an8}CHA SE-GYE

571
00:33:22,417 --> 00:33:23,585
Hello?

572
00:33:23,668 --> 00:33:26,087
<i>Cha Se-gye, it is I, Shin Seo-ri.</i>

573
00:33:28,215 --> 00:33:29,925
Is Grandfather okay?

574
00:33:30,008 --> 00:33:31,301
He's fine, of course.

575
00:33:31,384 --> 00:33:32,886
<i>He's full of energy.</i>

576
00:33:32,969 --> 00:33:34,429
He was worried about you,

577
00:33:34,513 --> 00:33:36,431
but I told him you were perfectly fine.

578
00:33:37,766 --> 00:33:39,184
He asked that you visit soon.

579
00:33:41,144 --> 00:33:42,771
He asked for me?

580
00:33:47,359 --> 00:33:48,777
Then, before that,

581
00:33:50,195 --> 00:33:51,530
should we maybe

582
00:33:52,197 --> 00:33:53,740
go somewhere nice tomorrow?

583
00:33:53,823 --> 00:33:55,575
-Somewhere nice?
<i>-You know,</i>

584
00:33:56,201 --> 00:33:58,537
we have not been on a proper date yet.

585
00:33:58,620 --> 00:34:00,830
<i>Last time, we only went</i>
<i>where I wanted to go.</i>

586
00:34:00,914 --> 00:34:02,290
<i>So this time,</i>

587
00:34:02,374 --> 00:34:04,251
let us go where you want to go.

588
00:34:05,168 --> 00:34:06,294
I shall follow you anywhere.

589
00:34:06,378 --> 00:34:08,547
Who knows where I might take you?

590
00:34:09,881 --> 00:34:11,007
So bold.

591
00:34:11,591 --> 00:34:12,926
Anyway,

592
00:34:13,009 --> 00:34:14,511
let us go somewhere tomorrow.

593
00:34:15,011 --> 00:34:16,555
<i>Take the night to think about where.</i>

594
00:34:17,889 --> 00:34:18,765
Hello?

595
00:34:20,100 --> 00:34:21,101
Jeez.

596
00:34:21,643 --> 00:34:23,562
So aggressive.

597
00:34:24,104 --> 00:34:25,438
I was planning to steal you away.

598
00:34:29,150 --> 00:34:30,443
How could you beat me to it?

599
00:34:38,868 --> 00:34:40,120
Was I sleepwalking?

600
00:34:41,538 --> 00:34:43,373
How do you like your hair today?

601
00:34:43,456 --> 00:34:44,583
I tried extra hard today.

602
00:34:46,418 --> 00:34:47,460
Give it here.

603
00:34:49,963 --> 00:34:51,715
Charity events

604
00:34:51,798 --> 00:34:54,092
call for that wholesome look.

605
00:34:54,175 --> 00:34:55,176
Yeah.

606
00:34:56,511 --> 00:34:57,846
Like this.

607
00:35:02,350 --> 00:35:03,685
Yeah? Done.

608
00:35:04,436 --> 00:35:06,521
-You can go.
-Okay.

609
00:35:09,733 --> 00:35:12,694
So your fling with Gong Tae-woo
was really just a rumor.

610
00:35:12,777 --> 00:35:15,488
I thought Han Min-hui was fake,
and you were the real deal.

611
00:35:15,572 --> 00:35:18,533
I thought you two were secretly dating
since filming that movie.

612
00:35:19,159 --> 00:35:21,536
Are you nuts? Why would I date
a thug like Gong Tae-woo?

613
00:35:21,620 --> 00:35:24,414
And I really don't like younger guys.

614
00:35:24,497 --> 00:35:25,373
Really?

615
00:35:25,457 --> 00:35:27,667
Hey, if you don't like younger guys,

616
00:35:27,751 --> 00:35:29,002
how about a half-celebrity?

617
00:35:29,711 --> 00:35:31,004
Shin Seo-ri's manager.

618
00:35:31,963 --> 00:35:33,256
You guys looked good together.

619
00:35:34,507 --> 00:35:35,759
Are you insane?

620
00:35:35,842 --> 00:35:37,427
Half-celebrity? Please.

621
00:35:37,510 --> 00:35:40,639
Even if he has some money,
a manager is still a manager.

622
00:35:41,181 --> 00:35:43,767
-Is he well off?
-What do his parents do?

623
00:35:43,850 --> 00:35:45,477
-What neighborhood?
-Well,

624
00:35:46,061 --> 00:35:47,646
I heard they run a business or something.

625
00:35:47,729 --> 00:35:50,315
I said no.
Why would I take over that business?

626
00:35:50,398 --> 00:35:51,608
I thought this was settled.

627
00:35:53,568 --> 00:35:55,403
He always has his nose up in the air.

628
00:35:55,487 --> 00:35:57,614
He'll never be a manager
with that attitude.

629
00:35:57,697 --> 00:35:58,698
I said no.

630
00:35:58,782 --> 00:36:01,618
I will never take over
Father's department store.

631
00:36:02,243 --> 00:36:03,203
Jeez.

632
00:36:06,373 --> 00:36:07,290
"Department store"?

633
00:36:07,916 --> 00:36:09,709
But a department store in the countryside?

634
00:36:09,793 --> 00:36:12,295
It's probably just a bit bigger
than a neighborhood supermarket?

635
00:36:12,379 --> 00:36:13,630
You don't know anything.

636
00:36:13,713 --> 00:36:16,299
Department stores in the countryside
are where it's at.

637
00:36:16,383 --> 00:36:18,176
They literally rake in the money.

638
00:36:18,259 --> 00:36:20,470
Yeah, a cousin of mine

639
00:36:20,553 --> 00:36:22,305
married the son of Gumi Department Store.

640
00:36:22,389 --> 00:36:23,973
She's totally set for life now.

641
00:36:24,057 --> 00:36:26,476
She rides supercars every day,
swapping them by color.

642
00:36:26,559 --> 00:36:28,520
Shin Seo-ri, that sly fox.

643
00:36:28,603 --> 00:36:30,563
She's been sitting on that golden ticket?

644
00:36:32,565 --> 00:36:34,693
I told you no.

645
00:36:34,776 --> 00:36:36,903
I'm not doing it. I won't.

646
00:36:38,655 --> 00:36:41,783
This punk always hangs up on me.

647
00:36:41,866 --> 00:36:42,867
Ma'am, how much is this?

648
00:36:42,951 --> 00:36:44,285
Didn't you see our sign?

649
00:36:44,369 --> 00:36:46,538
Everything here is a thousand won.

650
00:36:46,621 --> 00:36:49,999
THOUSAND WON DEPARTMENT STORE

651
00:36:50,083 --> 00:36:51,835
Hey, Mr. Department Store is here.

652
00:37:11,521 --> 00:37:12,731
What are you guys doing?

653
00:37:59,319 --> 00:38:01,362
I thought you didn't like it,
but you're wearing it.

654
00:38:04,157 --> 00:38:06,201
When did I say I did not like it?

655
00:38:06,284 --> 00:38:07,452
I just called it a leash.

656
00:38:07,535 --> 00:38:10,497
But where are we going right now?

657
00:38:11,080 --> 00:38:13,041
Should I have packed an overnight bag?

658
00:38:16,377 --> 00:38:18,087
Who's the devilish one now?

659
00:38:19,130 --> 00:38:22,217
After a night at my place,
an overnight trip is nothing now?

660
00:38:23,843 --> 00:38:25,553
What are you talking about?

661
00:38:27,597 --> 00:38:29,682
We'll have to save
the overnight for next time.

662
00:38:29,766 --> 00:38:31,518
Just think of today as meeting the family.

663
00:38:32,560 --> 00:38:33,436
Meeting the family?

664
00:38:33,520 --> 00:38:34,938
We're on our way to see my mom.

665
00:38:37,774 --> 00:38:41,152
REST IN PEACE, HAN HYE-SEON

666
00:38:45,240 --> 00:38:46,366
Well?

667
00:38:47,534 --> 00:38:49,661
-Isn't my mom beautiful?
-Yeah.

668
00:38:51,079 --> 00:38:53,623
Incredibly beautiful and elegant.

669
00:38:53,706 --> 00:38:56,167
I never understood why guys
wanted their families

670
00:38:56,251 --> 00:38:57,961
to meet their girlfriends,

671
00:38:58,044 --> 00:38:59,754
but now I do.

672
00:39:00,380 --> 00:39:01,923
I wanted to show you off.

673
00:39:02,715 --> 00:39:04,259
My pretty girlfriend.

674
00:39:05,385 --> 00:39:06,803
You should have told me beforehand.

675
00:39:07,679 --> 00:39:09,097
I would have dressed up nicer.

676
00:39:09,180 --> 00:39:10,557
You're perfect.

677
00:39:10,640 --> 00:39:12,058
How much nicer could you look?

678
00:39:12,141 --> 00:39:13,852
Are you trying to show my mom up?

679
00:39:14,394 --> 00:39:16,187
Mom has something to say. Hold on.

680
00:39:19,858 --> 00:39:20,984
She says she's prettier.

681
00:39:21,526 --> 00:39:22,777
She says not to worry.

682
00:39:37,250 --> 00:39:39,669
This is the last place I came
with Mom when I was little.

683
00:39:39,752 --> 00:39:41,754
Looking at it now, it's so tiny.

684
00:39:42,922 --> 00:39:44,632
Why did you never come back as an adult?

685
00:39:45,550 --> 00:39:46,843
Worried you might think of her?

686
00:39:50,597 --> 00:39:51,598
No.

687
00:39:54,267 --> 00:39:55,435
I was afraid I'd get weak.

688
00:39:56,936 --> 00:39:59,272
Thinking of Mom just makes me
feel some kind of way.

689
00:40:01,065 --> 00:40:02,442
It brings me down sometimes.

690
00:40:04,027 --> 00:40:05,737
Mom was pretty sick when I was young.

691
00:40:06,404 --> 00:40:08,406
But she lied to me.

692
00:40:09,198 --> 00:40:10,491
She said she'd get healthy

693
00:40:10,575 --> 00:40:12,201
and come back for me.

694
00:40:13,870 --> 00:40:14,913
She told me to wait.

695
00:40:26,174 --> 00:40:27,050
Se-gye.

696
00:40:29,385 --> 00:40:30,303
Cha Se-gye.

697
00:40:34,223 --> 00:40:35,224
Come here, Se-gye.

698
00:40:44,150 --> 00:40:45,485
My dear Se-gye.

699
00:40:45,568 --> 00:40:46,986
Just wait a little bit.

700
00:40:50,698 --> 00:40:52,283
I'll come back for you.

701
00:40:52,825 --> 00:40:56,454
<i>I only realized much later</i>
<i>that she couldn't come for me.</i>

702
00:40:57,580 --> 00:40:59,207
<i>But I didn't know that at the time.</i>

703
00:40:59,290 --> 00:41:02,168
I just sat by that window,
waiting for her every day.

704
00:41:02,251 --> 00:41:03,336
Before waiting some more.

705
00:41:08,257 --> 00:41:10,343
Would it have been better
if I'd known the truth?

706
00:41:15,139 --> 00:41:16,849
I don't even know anymore.

707
00:41:19,060 --> 00:41:20,728
I think knowing the truth is better.

708
00:41:23,022 --> 00:41:25,400
-What?
-Because waiting without knowing the end…

709
00:41:27,735 --> 00:41:28,820
is just too hard.

710
00:41:35,535 --> 00:41:36,828
Cha Se-gye.

711
00:41:40,039 --> 00:41:42,542
I do not want to lie to you.

712
00:41:42,625 --> 00:41:44,961
I do not want to make you wait endlessly.

713
00:41:45,628 --> 00:41:47,422
That is why I am telling you this.

714
00:41:49,549 --> 00:41:50,842
I am going back.

715
00:41:52,760 --> 00:41:54,012
Going back?

716
00:41:58,182 --> 00:41:59,517
I have to go back

717
00:42:00,393 --> 00:42:01,602
to where I came from.

718
00:42:09,068 --> 00:42:12,363
So let us do everything we can,
starting today.

719
00:42:12,447 --> 00:42:14,907
One by one, so we do not have regrets.

720
00:42:18,703 --> 00:42:19,871
What is this?

721
00:42:19,954 --> 00:42:21,289
Are you making fun of me?

722
00:42:21,956 --> 00:42:23,332
I believed all this nonsense

723
00:42:23,416 --> 00:42:25,835
about reincarnation
and transcending time and space,

724
00:42:26,502 --> 00:42:27,628
and now you're leaving?

725
00:42:28,504 --> 00:42:29,922
You're just going to leave?

726
00:42:32,592 --> 00:42:33,593
Cha Se-gye.

727
00:42:33,676 --> 00:42:35,970
At least try to make some sense.

728
00:42:36,054 --> 00:42:38,723
If you're leaving, when are you going?
In a month? Two months?

729
00:42:40,349 --> 00:42:42,185
-That is--
-Why? Is there no deadline?

730
00:42:42,268 --> 00:42:43,770
Haven't you set a date?

731
00:42:44,520 --> 00:42:46,439
I am not sure either.

732
00:42:47,148 --> 00:42:48,983
Probably around two weeks.

733
00:42:51,402 --> 00:42:53,654
-I guess there is one.
-I know this is hard for you.

734
00:42:54,197 --> 00:42:55,448
I know it very well.

735
00:42:55,948 --> 00:42:58,868
That is why I'm not hiding it
and telling you the truth for your sake.

736
00:42:58,951 --> 00:43:00,286
For my sake?

737
00:43:00,369 --> 00:43:03,331
So you asked me out on a date today
to tell me that nonsense?

738
00:43:04,082 --> 00:43:05,083
You…

739
00:43:06,584 --> 00:43:07,710
Do you think…

740
00:43:09,712 --> 00:43:11,380
it is easy for me to tell you this?

741
00:43:13,216 --> 00:43:15,676
Then what do you want? Applause?

742
00:43:15,760 --> 00:43:18,179
Should I get you a palanquin
so you can return in glory?

743
00:43:18,262 --> 00:43:20,640
What did you possibly expect from me

744
00:43:20,723 --> 00:43:22,725
when you came to me with such nonsense?

745
00:43:24,310 --> 00:43:25,937
-You…
-Why mess with me like this

746
00:43:26,020 --> 00:43:27,939
if you were just going to leave anyway?

747
00:43:28,022 --> 00:43:30,733
You turned someone barely holding it
together into a lovesick moron.

748
00:43:30,817 --> 00:43:31,943
Right now, I…

749
00:43:32,026 --> 00:43:33,152
No, you can't go.

750
00:43:34,070 --> 00:43:35,404
I refuse, so just know that.

751
00:43:35,488 --> 00:43:36,614
Cha Se-gye.

752
00:43:37,782 --> 00:43:38,658
No.

753
00:43:39,867 --> 00:43:42,703
I'm the crazy one for believing
everything you said until now.

754
00:43:44,122 --> 00:43:45,623
We're going to see a doctor tomorrow.

755
00:43:45,706 --> 00:43:47,500
We'll get an EEG or whatever.

756
00:43:47,583 --> 00:43:50,086
Just get a full checkup,
and then we can talk.

757
00:43:50,753 --> 00:43:51,838
This is just…

758
00:43:53,631 --> 00:43:54,841
Damn it.

759
00:44:09,605 --> 00:44:11,482
I do not want to leave either.

760
00:44:13,651 --> 00:44:15,862
I want to stay by your side.

761
00:45:10,872 --> 00:45:13,336
{\an8}MY AMAZING FAN

762
00:45:25,848 --> 00:45:27,975
<i>If only I could take it with me.</i>

763
00:45:28,059 --> 00:45:31,020
<i>Then I would have something to look at</i>

764
00:45:31,103 --> 00:45:33,105
<i>from time to time.</i>

765
00:45:55,044 --> 00:45:58,339
From now on, I want all the money
coming to me to be deposited here.

766
00:45:58,422 --> 00:45:59,507
Please.

767
00:46:04,345 --> 00:46:06,138
NAM OK-SUN
SONGJIN GENERAL HOSPITAL

768
00:46:07,056 --> 00:46:08,432
Are you going somewhere?

769
00:46:08,516 --> 00:46:11,894
Now that the drama is over,
are you going on a trip or something?

770
00:46:12,937 --> 00:46:13,896
A trip?

771
00:46:13,980 --> 00:46:15,523
Actually, I'm glad you're here today.

772
00:46:16,065 --> 00:46:18,943
You should have this picture.

773
00:46:19,026 --> 00:46:20,152
Picture?

774
00:46:21,404 --> 00:46:23,155
I found it while cleaning the storage.

775
00:46:35,084 --> 00:46:36,752
I'll pay you back soon.

776
00:46:36,836 --> 00:46:38,796
Seo-ri, my dearest daughter.

777
00:46:38,879 --> 00:46:40,339
When you wake up from your nap,

778
00:46:41,257 --> 00:46:42,341
we should be home.

779
00:46:44,719 --> 00:46:46,220
I was right.

780
00:46:47,763 --> 00:46:49,348
That was a childhood memory.

781
00:46:49,432 --> 00:46:50,641
Do you remember?

782
00:46:55,855 --> 00:46:57,106
She will be back soon.

783
00:46:58,399 --> 00:46:59,942
<i>Once I am gone.</i>

784
00:47:03,237 --> 00:47:05,323
<i>My name is Dan-sim.</i>

785
00:47:05,406 --> 00:47:06,991
<i>Kang Dan-sim.</i>

786
00:47:07,074 --> 00:47:09,076
That tone…

787
00:47:13,831 --> 00:47:15,875
What is your name?

788
00:47:15,958 --> 00:47:17,793
My name is Dan-sim.

789
00:47:17,877 --> 00:47:18,836
Kang Dan-sim.

790
00:47:21,756 --> 00:47:24,383
Just as I thought. Her tone…

791
00:47:25,968 --> 00:47:27,636
I don't think it's Her Highness.

792
00:47:30,389 --> 00:47:32,308
Maybe she's not going back?

793
00:47:32,391 --> 00:47:33,434
<i>Here is our next story.</i>

794
00:47:33,517 --> 00:47:36,479
<i>According to the BBC,</i>
<i>five Joseon-era artifacts</i>

795
00:47:36,562 --> 00:47:40,024
<i>currently held at the British Museum</i>
<i>are set to be repatriated.</i>

796
00:47:40,107 --> 00:47:43,027
<i>Among the items to be returned</i>
<i>is reportedly a diary belonging</i>

797
00:47:43,110 --> 00:47:46,072
<i>to Grand Prince Cheongheon,</i>
<i>the younger brother of Anjong of Joseon,</i>

798
00:47:46,155 --> 00:47:49,075
<i>who is also known</i>
<i>as the "ill-fated prince."</i>

799
00:47:49,700 --> 00:47:51,327
<i>The diary is currently…</i>

800
00:47:51,410 --> 00:47:53,727
How does it feel to be heading
into the heart of the enemy?

801
00:47:53,829 --> 00:47:56,540
<i>-…a painting of a court lady…</i>
-For a formal meeting and not an ambush.

802
00:47:56,624 --> 00:47:57,875
No reason to fuss.

803
00:47:57,958 --> 00:47:59,668
When did feelings get in the way of work?

804
00:47:59,752 --> 00:48:02,505
<i>…lending weight</i>
<i>to the academic hypothesis.</i>

805
00:48:06,342 --> 00:48:07,385
Step on it.

806
00:48:08,344 --> 00:48:10,596
Choi Mun-do must be
waiting anxiously for us.

807
00:48:11,389 --> 00:48:13,474
<i>I would like to thank</i>
<i>all the executives for attending</i>

808
00:48:13,557 --> 00:48:15,643
<i>the first official meeting</i>
<i>for Songjin Resort today.</i>

809
00:48:15,726 --> 00:48:18,253
The fact that you took time
out of your busy schedules

810
00:48:18,353 --> 00:48:21,607
shows that you support this project
and believe this will bring forth

811
00:48:21,690 --> 00:48:23,984
a new era for Chail.
I appreciate it greatly.

812
00:48:25,778 --> 00:48:27,863
Now, shall we begin the meeting?

813
00:48:34,286 --> 00:48:36,163
Wow…

814
00:48:36,247 --> 00:48:38,249
They're ostracizing me now.

815
00:48:38,332 --> 00:48:40,668
Ms. Nam Ok-sun's bills are fully paid.

816
00:48:40,751 --> 00:48:43,587
She's registered for automatic payments
under Mr. Cha Se-gye.

817
00:48:43,671 --> 00:48:45,673
We actually needed
her guardian's consent anyway.

818
00:48:45,756 --> 00:48:47,425
You can do it now.

819
00:48:52,138 --> 00:48:53,264
Then this too.

820
00:48:54,056 --> 00:48:55,474
Have this account be linked as well.

821
00:48:55,558 --> 00:48:59,186
So she can be well taken care of
even if you cannot reach me.

822
00:48:59,270 --> 00:49:00,855
Please.

823
00:49:07,945 --> 00:49:11,157
<i>She's registered for automatic payments</i>
<i>under Mr. Cha Se-gye.</i>

824
00:49:12,950 --> 00:49:15,578
Why mess with me like this
if you were just going to leave anyway?

825
00:49:16,370 --> 00:49:18,956
You turned someone barely holding it
together into a lovesick moron.

826
00:49:19,039 --> 00:49:20,291
<i>Right now, I…</i>

827
00:49:20,916 --> 00:49:22,042
You jerk.

828
00:49:22,877 --> 00:49:24,128
How could you say that?

829
00:49:26,172 --> 00:49:29,467
Then again, I am the worst one of all.

830
00:49:30,759 --> 00:49:32,428
Saying goodbye with a smile…

831
00:49:34,346 --> 00:49:35,931
I am one greedy wench.

832
00:50:03,000 --> 00:50:04,126
She is not in her room.

833
00:50:04,210 --> 00:50:05,377
The patient is missing!

834
00:50:05,461 --> 00:50:06,921
No need to panic.

835
00:50:07,004 --> 00:50:10,216
She didn't disappear. She just went
for a short walk right out front.

836
00:50:11,842 --> 00:50:14,637
Ma'am, do you have a moment?

837
00:50:14,720 --> 00:50:16,805
You should speak to her doctor.

838
00:50:30,861 --> 00:50:32,530
Why are you out in the cold?

839
00:50:33,239 --> 00:50:34,365
What if you catch a cold?

840
00:50:34,448 --> 00:50:37,409
It's fun sitting here like this.

841
00:50:38,118 --> 00:50:42,248
Watching people get on and off the bus
keeps me from getting bored.

842
00:50:42,957 --> 00:50:44,083
Why?

843
00:50:45,167 --> 00:50:47,169
Do you like seeing people out and about?

844
00:50:49,421 --> 00:50:50,589
No, it's not that.

845
00:50:51,715 --> 00:50:53,300
Actually…

846
00:50:55,135 --> 00:50:58,556
my dream when I was a kid
was to be a driver.

847
00:51:00,599 --> 00:51:03,602
Other kids wanted to be the bus guides.

848
00:51:03,686 --> 00:51:06,605
But I really wanted to be the driver.

849
00:51:07,690 --> 00:51:10,859
Gosh. Driving all day in a car,

850
00:51:11,402 --> 00:51:13,279
having a blast,

851
00:51:13,362 --> 00:51:16,532
making money, and seeing the world
to my heart's content.

852
00:51:16,615 --> 00:51:18,450
Living life on your own terms is enviable.

853
00:51:19,076 --> 00:51:21,453
I was so envious of that.

854
00:51:21,537 --> 00:51:23,163
A little disappointed I couldn't.

855
00:51:26,709 --> 00:51:28,627
Now, the next item on the agenda

856
00:51:28,711 --> 00:51:30,713
is the most important issue.

857
00:51:34,300 --> 00:51:35,384
Securing the site.

858
00:51:35,467 --> 00:51:37,344
Earlier at the groundbreaking ceremony,

859
00:51:37,428 --> 00:51:39,763
press releases went out saying
the site was fully secured,

860
00:51:39,847 --> 00:51:42,600
but the plot near the resort entrance
hasn't been purchased yet.

861
00:51:42,683 --> 00:51:45,978
The site purchase needs to be completed
before construction begins,

862
00:51:46,061 --> 00:51:48,105
but the owner of this plot
is very stubborn.

863
00:51:48,188 --> 00:51:49,648
You don't worry about that.

864
00:51:50,441 --> 00:51:52,818
The head of our new TF team
will take care of it.

865
00:51:53,360 --> 00:51:54,903
Isn't that right, Mr. Cha?

866
00:51:59,116 --> 00:52:00,492
What?

867
00:52:00,576 --> 00:52:03,829
I guess it hasn't been shared
with the executives yet.

868
00:52:03,912 --> 00:52:05,706
Thanks to Mr. Cha Se-gye's connections,

869
00:52:05,789 --> 00:52:08,584
we have successfully signed
a contract with the restaurant owner.

870
00:52:13,255 --> 00:52:14,465
SEORI'S NOODLE SHOP

871
00:52:14,548 --> 00:52:16,800
Thanks to the legwork he put in,

872
00:52:16,884 --> 00:52:19,428
we have finally secured 100% of the site.

873
00:52:20,179 --> 00:52:21,639
Please give him a round of applause.

874
00:52:38,530 --> 00:52:39,823
That's a good age.

875
00:52:41,283 --> 00:52:42,785
But they don't know that.

876
00:52:43,702 --> 00:52:46,491
-I'll have <i>tteokbokki.</i>
-Let's add one serving of beef brisket.

877
00:52:46,580 --> 00:52:49,833
I thought I'd be
young like that forever too.

878
00:52:49,917 --> 00:52:53,379
But I blinked, and I became an old lady.

879
00:52:54,004 --> 00:52:56,006
I was so busy rolling all that dough.

880
00:52:56,882 --> 00:52:58,592
I didn't know my hair had gone gray.

881
00:53:02,054 --> 00:53:04,098
But still,

882
00:53:04,181 --> 00:53:06,600
that doesn't mean
I didn't like running the restaurant.

883
00:53:06,684 --> 00:53:09,478
Watching kids enjoy my noodles

884
00:53:09,561 --> 00:53:10,938
made me full too.

885
00:53:11,438 --> 00:53:13,899
That's why I didn't stop working.

886
00:53:16,485 --> 00:53:17,444
But now,

887
00:53:18,237 --> 00:53:19,780
that's all over too.

888
00:53:21,740 --> 00:53:23,867
I should slowly start wrapping things up.

889
00:53:25,744 --> 00:53:27,996
Is it because
of the restaurant demolition?

890
00:53:28,497 --> 00:53:29,998
I will try to take care of that--

891
00:53:30,082 --> 00:53:31,709
No, look at me.

892
00:53:31,792 --> 00:53:33,168
How do I look to you?

893
00:53:34,002 --> 00:53:35,671
Do you think I can run a restaurant again?

894
00:53:37,256 --> 00:53:40,342
<i>Ms. Nam Ok-sun is not doing well.</i>

895
00:53:40,426 --> 00:53:42,094
While we couldn't reach you,

896
00:53:42,177 --> 00:53:44,346
her cognitive function
has dropped rapidly.

897
00:53:44,430 --> 00:53:46,235
As well as her physical function.

898
00:53:46,306 --> 00:53:48,684
You should probably prepare yourself…

899
00:53:49,685 --> 00:53:50,686
Prepare myself?

900
00:53:51,311 --> 00:53:53,522
<i>She doesn't have much time left.</i>

901
00:53:54,940 --> 00:53:57,693
Of course you can. Why not?

902
00:53:59,153 --> 00:54:00,237
No.

903
00:54:00,821 --> 00:54:02,906
I only held on to it all this time

904
00:54:02,990 --> 00:54:05,159
out of greed and sentiment.

905
00:54:09,413 --> 00:54:10,789
It's okay.

906
00:54:11,498 --> 00:54:12,750
Don't worry about it.

907
00:54:14,334 --> 00:54:16,545
Hey, it's cold out today.

908
00:54:17,254 --> 00:54:20,215
Why are you wearing such thin clothes?

909
00:54:22,259 --> 00:54:24,803
Your hands are so cold. Jeez.

910
00:54:25,554 --> 00:54:26,597
My granddaughter

911
00:54:27,806 --> 00:54:30,058
always goes around with her hands
freezing like this too.

912
00:54:30,726 --> 00:54:32,269
In a little bit,

913
00:54:32,770 --> 00:54:33,729
the sun will set.

914
00:54:34,688 --> 00:54:36,148
She's late.

915
00:54:54,208 --> 00:54:55,834
Miss, you must be cold.

916
00:54:55,918 --> 00:54:59,671
Here. Put this on, at least. Go on.

917
00:55:01,340 --> 00:55:02,549
Here you go.

918
00:55:02,633 --> 00:55:05,511
I'll lend it to you until my bus comes.

919
00:55:06,470 --> 00:55:08,555
My granddaughter bought this for me.

920
00:55:09,264 --> 00:55:10,390
How is it?

921
00:55:10,474 --> 00:55:15,062
Doesn't it feel a bit better wrapped up
all warm and cozy like this?

922
00:55:16,021 --> 00:55:17,356
It's pretty.

923
00:55:18,816 --> 00:55:20,192
No, I am…

924
00:55:23,654 --> 00:55:25,113
I am not…

925
00:55:28,075 --> 00:55:29,409
Miss, why are you crying?

926
00:55:29,493 --> 00:55:32,079
Are you upset about something?

927
00:55:34,248 --> 00:55:38,460
Oh my. You'll lose your energy
if you cry like this.

928
00:55:38,544 --> 00:55:40,796
Please don't cry.

929
00:55:48,470 --> 00:55:50,222
What's wrong with me?

930
00:55:53,642 --> 00:55:56,937
Why does my chest hurt so much?

931
00:56:00,899 --> 00:56:03,235
Don't cry, okay?

932
00:56:05,320 --> 00:56:07,990
Don't cry…

933
00:56:22,421 --> 00:56:23,755
It hurts.

934
00:56:23,839 --> 00:56:26,633
Don't cry…

935
00:56:28,844 --> 00:56:30,220
Don't cry.

936
00:56:32,264 --> 00:56:34,391
Don't cry.

937
00:56:36,393 --> 00:56:38,437
Don't cry.

938
00:56:42,357 --> 00:56:44,234
You can't go in right now…

939
00:56:55,871 --> 00:56:57,122
So this is what you wanted?

940
00:56:57,205 --> 00:56:59,333
You just wanted me to walk out on my own?

941
00:57:00,042 --> 00:57:01,919
No, why would you leave?

942
00:57:02,002 --> 00:57:03,754
I already told the Chairman

943
00:57:03,837 --> 00:57:06,965
to watch closely as you prove yourself
with the chance you were given.

944
00:57:07,049 --> 00:57:08,175
To see

945
00:57:08,800 --> 00:57:10,302
what our Crown Prince chooses.

946
00:57:10,385 --> 00:57:11,511
What?

947
00:57:11,595 --> 00:57:13,013
I guess you don't know this yet,

948
00:57:13,096 --> 00:57:15,390
but I'm more compassionate than I look.

949
00:57:15,474 --> 00:57:16,600
Look at me right now.

950
00:57:16,683 --> 00:57:19,353
I'm giving you a chance
to regain Uncle's trust.

951
00:57:19,436 --> 00:57:20,938
And also a chance

952
00:57:21,772 --> 00:57:23,315
to win love.

953
00:57:23,398 --> 00:57:25,025
Whatever you do, you'll gain something.

954
00:57:25,108 --> 00:57:27,439
Is there a reason to be this mad at me?

955
00:57:28,362 --> 00:57:30,072
Look at you having a blast.

956
00:57:30,155 --> 00:57:32,074
Your eyes light up
when you play with people.

957
00:57:32,157 --> 00:57:33,909
Yeah, I'll admit it.

958
00:57:34,534 --> 00:57:35,869
It is fun.

959
00:57:40,082 --> 00:57:42,542
But you should probably hurry up now.

960
00:57:45,087 --> 00:57:46,922
If you decide to choose her,

961
00:57:47,422 --> 00:57:48,590
you don't have much time left.

962
00:57:48,674 --> 00:57:49,633
What time?

963
00:57:49,716 --> 00:57:52,386
The demolition team should be heading
to the site right now.

964
00:57:53,303 --> 00:57:55,013
They'll arrive before sunset.

965
00:57:59,351 --> 00:58:02,479
<i>I told them to demolish</i>
<i>the entrance plot first.</i>

966
00:58:02,562 --> 00:58:06,108
To wipe out
that messy commercial area first.

967
00:58:07,359 --> 00:58:08,443
Well?

968
00:58:08,527 --> 00:58:10,153
Shouldn't you go and check on her?

969
00:58:10,237 --> 00:58:11,655
You bastard.

970
00:58:15,492 --> 00:58:17,119
There we go.

971
00:58:17,202 --> 00:58:18,620
This is the Cha Se-gye I know.

972
00:58:18,704 --> 00:58:22,249
Throwing punches without thinking
and cursing up a storm.

973
00:58:22,332 --> 00:58:24,251
Only knowing how to throw a tantrum.

974
00:58:24,334 --> 00:58:25,585
You really

975
00:58:26,545 --> 00:58:29,172
have never wanted for anything.

976
00:58:29,756 --> 00:58:32,759
Just a kid running wild
without knowing how the world works.

977
00:58:54,197 --> 00:58:55,449
Fine.

978
00:58:57,701 --> 00:58:58,744
Do whatever you want.

979
00:59:01,038 --> 00:59:04,249
Do whatever you want with the company.
Tear it apart or destroy it.

980
00:59:04,332 --> 00:59:07,586
But that messy restaurant spot
isn't important at all.

981
00:59:08,879 --> 00:59:10,756
You can easily just leave it alone.

982
00:59:12,591 --> 00:59:15,135
I haven't done a single thing right
for that woman.

983
00:59:15,218 --> 00:59:17,095
So just leave that alone.

984
00:59:19,222 --> 00:59:20,265
Is that an order?

985
00:59:21,600 --> 00:59:22,851
Or a favor?

986
00:59:24,269 --> 00:59:25,479
Pick one.

987
00:59:30,442 --> 00:59:31,985
If you step on me, I'll let you.

988
00:59:32,486 --> 00:59:33,987
If you tell me to bow, I will.

989
00:59:34,071 --> 00:59:35,489
So just let that one thing go.

990
00:59:36,198 --> 00:59:38,408
To us, it may be a messy,
insignificant restaurant,

991
00:59:38,492 --> 00:59:41,203
but for someone else,
it's their home and their life.

992
00:59:43,288 --> 00:59:44,372
So just spare them that.

993
00:59:46,374 --> 00:59:47,793
I'm begging you.

994
00:59:56,009 --> 00:59:58,303
I thought you were a kid,
but you're a man.

995
00:59:59,930 --> 01:00:02,182
Now we can finally talk.

996
01:00:02,265 --> 01:00:03,517
Right?

997
01:00:05,352 --> 01:00:06,812
But you know what, Se-gye?

998
01:00:08,021 --> 01:00:10,649
I gave the demolition team
special instructions.

999
01:00:12,067 --> 01:00:14,361
No matter who, no matter when…

1000
01:00:14,903 --> 01:00:16,446
No matter what happens,

1001
01:00:17,155 --> 01:00:19,282
they are to proceed.

1002
01:00:21,326 --> 01:00:22,619
Too bad.

1003
01:00:26,164 --> 01:00:27,207
Damn it.

1004
01:00:30,669 --> 01:00:32,504
Damn child.

1005
01:00:43,348 --> 01:00:44,266
Director Jang.

1006
01:00:46,852 --> 01:00:48,145
Please follow me.

1007
01:01:06,163 --> 01:01:07,205
Director Jang.

1008
01:01:14,671 --> 01:01:16,256
Jang Seok-ho!

1009
01:01:18,842 --> 01:01:20,010
Your Highness!

1010
01:01:21,303 --> 01:01:22,846
-Excuse me.
-Where did she go?

1011
01:01:25,098 --> 01:01:27,225
-What are you doing there?
-Her Highness.

1012
01:01:27,309 --> 01:01:29,936
No, I mean. Where did Seo-ri go?

1013
01:01:30,020 --> 01:01:31,688
She went to see her grandmother. Why?

1014
01:01:32,397 --> 01:01:33,982
I need to tell her this.

1015
01:01:34,065 --> 01:01:36,276
I need to let her know
as soon as possible.

1016
01:01:36,359 --> 01:01:38,528
Why isn't she picking up her damn phone?

1017
01:01:38,612 --> 01:01:41,072
What are you talking about?
You can tell me.

1018
01:01:41,990 --> 01:01:42,908
No. It's--

1019
01:01:42,991 --> 01:01:44,826
I'm her manager.

1020
01:01:46,578 --> 01:01:47,787
Just tell me.

1021
01:01:48,480 --> 01:01:50,994
SEORI'S NOODLE SHOP

1022
01:02:00,467 --> 01:02:01,788
2025 TO 2026

1023
01:02:20,779 --> 01:02:22,239
So meticulous.

1024
01:02:27,452 --> 01:02:29,204
<i>You know, I've been feeling good recently.</i>

1025
01:02:29,287 --> 01:02:32,082
<i>Everything hit the fan,</i>
<i>but strangely, I feel good.</i>

1026
01:02:32,165 --> 01:02:33,458
<i>You idiot.</i>

1027
01:02:33,541 --> 01:02:35,252
I think I needed something to hold on to.

1028
01:02:35,335 --> 01:02:37,754
I had to hold on to something
to feel like I was alive.

1029
01:02:38,964 --> 01:02:41,007
<i>All caught up in your own damn feelings.</i>

1030
01:02:41,508 --> 01:02:42,509
I finally get it.

1031
01:02:43,176 --> 01:02:44,386
What's really important.

1032
01:02:44,886 --> 01:02:48,098
What I truly need.

1033
01:02:49,349 --> 01:02:51,851
<i>You don't know anything.</i>

1034
01:02:52,560 --> 01:02:53,645
I just…

1035
01:02:54,688 --> 01:02:56,273
I just need you.

1036
01:02:57,983 --> 01:03:01,069
<i>I was completely oblivious to the despair</i>

1037
01:03:02,362 --> 01:03:03,905
<i>you've shouldered alone.</i>

1038
01:03:08,535 --> 01:03:10,745
<i>It's not cabbage. It's basically gold now.</i>

1039
01:03:10,829 --> 01:03:13,873
<i>It's so ridiculous.</i>
<i>I might just start farming it myself.</i>

1040
01:03:15,417 --> 01:03:17,502
<i>The sign across the street says</i>
<i>they're the original.</i>

1041
01:03:17,585 --> 01:03:20,797
<i>The original </i>kalguksu?
<i>They're making me laugh nonstop.</i>

1042
01:03:21,840 --> 01:03:23,508
Half of this is just swearing.

1043
01:03:25,051 --> 01:03:26,678
Such a foul mouth she has.

1044
01:03:28,513 --> 01:03:29,723
<i>Oh my, that little brat.</i>

1045
01:03:29,806 --> 01:03:32,600
<i>When I told her to eat some carrots,</i>
<i>she threw a fit and pinched me.</i>

1046
01:03:32,684 --> 01:03:34,394
<i>For a little thing,</i>
<i>she's got a strong grip.</i>

1047
01:03:44,529 --> 01:03:46,156
Grandma, I'm home.

1048
01:03:46,239 --> 01:03:48,658
My sweet girl. You're home.

1049
01:03:49,367 --> 01:03:50,618
-Let's eat some carrots!
-What?

1050
01:03:50,702 --> 01:03:52,203
-Let's eat some carrots!
-I said no!

1051
01:03:52,287 --> 01:03:53,496
-I don't want to!
-Come on!

1052
01:03:53,580 --> 01:03:54,497
I hate carrots.

1053
01:03:54,581 --> 01:03:57,334
That hurts! You little brat.

1054
01:03:57,417 --> 01:03:58,626
My goodness.

1055
01:04:08,136 --> 01:04:11,222
<i>My Seo-ri is on TV.</i>

1056
01:04:11,765 --> 01:04:14,225
<i>I was so excited that I gave</i>
<i>everything away for free today.</i>

1057
01:04:14,309 --> 01:04:15,977
Look at my sweet girl.

1058
01:04:16,061 --> 01:04:19,856
<i>I'm so glad Dong-seok took her to Seoul.</i>

1059
01:04:19,939 --> 01:04:21,941
<i>He should have taken her sooner.</i>

1060
01:04:23,276 --> 01:04:26,029
<i>My Seo-ri is on every time</i>
<i>I turn on the TV.</i>

1061
01:04:26,613 --> 01:04:28,740
<i>I mean, I'm happy about it,</i>

1062
01:04:29,866 --> 01:04:32,744
<i>but is she doing okay in school?</i>

1063
01:04:32,827 --> 01:04:33,953
<i>Is she eating well?</i>

1064
01:04:34,496 --> 01:04:37,040
<i>I'm worried because</i>
<i>she's as skinny as a skewer.</i>

1065
01:04:39,459 --> 01:04:41,002
<i>I miss you.</i>

1066
01:04:49,386 --> 01:04:50,261
2002 TO 2003

1067
01:04:56,768 --> 01:04:58,520
<i>Her belly is cold.</i>

1068
01:04:58,603 --> 01:05:01,231
<i>I'm worried because</i>
<i>she always has a stomachache.</i>

1069
01:05:02,190 --> 01:05:05,360
<i>I should brew</i>
<i>some herbal medicine for her.</i>

1070
01:05:08,154 --> 01:05:10,073
Grandma.

1071
01:05:10,156 --> 01:05:12,909
My tummy aches. Can I have a tummy rub?

1072
01:05:12,992 --> 01:05:14,702
Do you have a stomachache again?

1073
01:05:14,786 --> 01:05:15,829
Come here.

1074
01:05:16,413 --> 01:05:17,664
Oh my.

1075
01:05:17,747 --> 01:05:19,666
Grandma will give you her healing hands.

1076
01:05:19,749 --> 01:05:24,337
<i>Grandma's hands are healing hands</i>

1077
01:05:24,421 --> 01:05:27,715
<i>Seo-ri's tummy is a potbelly</i>

1078
01:05:27,799 --> 01:05:30,176
Hey! I don't have a potbelly!

1079
01:05:31,845 --> 01:05:36,015
<i>Grandma's hands are healing hands</i>

1080
01:05:36,599 --> 01:05:40,395
<i>Seo-ri's tummy is a potbelly</i>

1081
01:05:44,816 --> 01:05:46,025
<i>What is this?</i>

1082
01:05:48,695 --> 01:05:51,322
<i>They told me to wait.</i>

1083
01:05:53,700 --> 01:05:56,286
<i>They said they'd be right back.</i>

1084
01:05:58,830 --> 01:06:01,708
<i>They told me to wait here.</i>

1085
01:06:02,709 --> 01:06:04,043
What is wrong with me?

1086
01:06:05,003 --> 01:06:06,546
<i>But that's quite strange.</i>

1087
01:06:06,629 --> 01:06:09,424
<i>Childhood memories</i>
<i>should have been borne away</i>

1088
01:06:09,507 --> 01:06:10,884
<i>with the soul of the body's master.</i>

1089
01:06:10,967 --> 01:06:13,178
<i>How did they stay and get tangled up?</i>

1090
01:06:13,261 --> 01:06:15,430
Why do I keep…

1091
01:06:19,601 --> 01:06:23,146
<i>Right. This is not my body,</i>
<i>and those are not my memories.</i>

1092
01:06:23,897 --> 01:06:25,398
<i>How did they get tangled with my own?</i>

1093
01:06:25,482 --> 01:06:27,150
<i>I was just trapped again.</i>

1094
01:06:27,233 --> 01:06:28,651
<i>I was trapped.</i>

1095
01:06:28,735 --> 01:06:30,528
It felt like I was dying.

1096
01:06:31,446 --> 01:06:33,698
<i>The soul and memories are a pair.</i>

1097
01:06:33,781 --> 01:06:35,825
<i>They shouldn't be separated.</i>

1098
01:06:36,618 --> 01:06:38,161
<i>It feels like they are mine.</i>

1099
01:06:40,455 --> 01:06:42,040
<i>How does that make sense?</i>

1100
01:06:45,043 --> 01:06:46,044
<i>How?</i>

1101
01:06:47,003 --> 01:06:47,879
<i>Seo-ri.</i>

1102
01:06:50,089 --> 01:06:51,466
My sweet girl.

1103
01:06:52,800 --> 01:06:54,302
My sweet girl.

1104
01:06:56,638 --> 01:06:58,097
My sweet girl.

1105
01:06:58,806 --> 01:07:00,141
When are you coming?

1106
01:07:00,725 --> 01:07:04,562
<i>When is my sweet girl coming?</i>

1107
01:07:19,744 --> 01:07:21,162
<i>Seo-ri.</i>

1108
01:07:21,788 --> 01:07:23,164
<i>My sweet girl.</i>

1109
01:07:25,208 --> 01:07:26,501
Grandma!

1110
01:07:26,584 --> 01:07:27,669
Grandma.

1111
01:07:38,221 --> 01:07:41,849
<i>Seo-ri, my sweet girl.</i>

1112
01:07:41,933 --> 01:07:43,101
Grandma!

1113
01:07:44,269 --> 01:07:46,271
-Grandma, I'll be taller than you!
-Yeah.

1114
01:07:46,354 --> 01:07:47,230
Okay, let's make sure!

1115
01:07:47,313 --> 01:07:48,898
My sweet girl.

1116
01:07:48,982 --> 01:07:50,692
This is crazy!

1117
01:07:50,775 --> 01:07:51,693
Really?

1118
01:07:51,776 --> 01:07:54,279
My sweet girl. How exciting!

1119
01:07:55,947 --> 01:07:57,031
My sweet girl.

1120
01:08:00,410 --> 01:08:02,161
My sweet girl.

1121
01:08:10,920 --> 01:08:12,255
<i>Grandma.</i>

1122
01:08:23,057 --> 01:08:24,350
<i>That's not you.</i>

1123
01:08:26,227 --> 01:08:27,478
<i>You're just a fake.</i>

1124
01:08:27,562 --> 01:08:29,355
<i>Get out of my body.</i>

1125
01:08:31,524 --> 01:08:33,901
<i>No, I am not a fake.</i>

1126
01:08:35,445 --> 01:08:36,404
<i>I am…</i>

1127
01:08:37,322 --> 01:08:38,406
<i>My name is…</i>

1128
01:08:44,704 --> 01:08:45,747
<i>Shin Seo-ri.</i>

1129
01:09:20,573 --> 01:09:21,658
Just a little bit.

1130
01:09:23,951 --> 01:09:25,244
Just wait a little bit longer.

1131
01:09:50,561 --> 01:09:54,148
MY ROYAL NEMESIS

1132
01:10:24,760 --> 01:10:26,055
{\an8}I'm not letting you go anywhere.

1133
01:10:26,139 --> 01:10:27,432
{\an8}<i>I am not going back.</i>

1134
01:10:27,515 --> 01:10:29,934
{\an8}<i>Because I have returned to where I belong.</i>

1135
01:10:30,017 --> 01:10:31,949
{\an8}I'll put the brakes
on the resort development.

1136
01:10:32,028 --> 01:10:34,313
{\an8}I hear they're building an airport
next to the resort site.

1137
01:10:34,397 --> 01:10:36,649
{\an8}<i>-What about Seo-jun?</i>
<i>-Your driver picked him up.</i>

1138
01:10:36,733 --> 01:10:38,651
{\an8}<i>Your threat was loud and clear.</i>

1139
01:10:38,735 --> 01:10:40,778
{\an8}And you crossed a line you shouldn't have.

1140
01:10:40,862 --> 01:10:43,322
{\an8}<i>Her condition has rapidly deteriorated.</i>

1141
01:10:44,449 --> 01:10:45,366
{\an8}<i>Grandma.</i>

1142
01:10:45,450 --> 01:10:47,118
{\an8}<i>Tell me.</i>

1143
01:10:47,201 --> 01:10:48,703
{\an8}I will pay any price!

1144
01:10:48,786 --> 01:10:52,165
{\an8}<i>Even at the cost</i>
<i>of never returning here again?</i>

1145
01:10:55,170 --> 01:10:57,170
{\an8}Subtitle translation by Justin S. Kim
